<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> God reveals himself as Father in Scripture, and Jesus teaches us to relate to him with filial trust.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that God's name (&laquo;I AM&raquo;) reveals his being and his closeness.</li>
<li>Discover that God is Father from the Old Testament onward.</li>
<li>Know the radical novelty of Jesus: God is Abba, Daddy.</li>
<li>Interiorize that &laquo;God is Love&raquo; (1 Jn 4:8).</li>
<li>Live out filial trust as children, not as slaves.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;You did not receive a spirit of slavery to fall back into fear, but you received a spirit of adoption, through which we cry, 'Abba, Father!'&raquo; (Rom 8:15)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 198-231, 239-241, 268-271, 295-296</p>

</section>

